<h2 id="what-is-moosend" emoji="📬">What Is Moosend?</h2>

Moosend is a full-stack email marketing platform built for teams that need serious automation without a serious price tag. Launched in 2011 and now part of the Sitecore portfolio, it covers email campaigns, automation workflows, landing pages, subscription forms, and basic CRM functionality under one roof.

For travel agencies, the platform's standout capability is its <strong>behavior-triggered automation</strong>. When a subscriber browses your Bali itinerary three times without booking, Moosend can fire a targeted follow-up sequence automatically — the kind of logic that used to require enterprise tools or a dedicated developer.

<h2 id="what-is-aweber" emoji="📨">What Is AWeber?</h2>

AWeber has been around since 1998 and built its reputation on being the dependable, no-drama email tool for small businesses. It pioneered autoresponders, offers a large template library, and has long appealed to operators who want something that "just works" without a steep learning curve.

In 2026, AWeber still holds its own in deliverability and customer support, but the platform's automation capabilities lag behind newer competitors. For high-volume travel agencies running complex seasonal campaigns, those gaps start to matter.

<h2 id="our-experience" emoji="🧳">Our Experience Testing Both Tools</h2>

Our team has worked alongside travel agencies managing thousands of tour departures — from adventure operators running 400-seat group departures to boutique agencies handling 12-person luxury journeys. We've stress-tested both platforms across real campaign cycles: pre-season awareness pushes, last-minute availability fills, and post-trip review sequences.

We evaluated each tool on five criteria that matter specifically to travel operators: <strong>automation flexibility, segmentation depth, template quality for destination marketing, pricing at scale, and deliverability</strong>.

